#1.A hospital uses a deep learning model to classify medical images. A small grayscale image is represented by a 3 × 3 matrix of pixel intensities. Before classification, the image must be converted into a one-dimensional vector, and the total pixel intensity must be calculated. Write a Python program to flatten the image matrix into a one-dimensional vector and calculate the sum of all pixel intensities. Image matrix: A = [[10, 20, 30], [40, 50, 60], [70, 80, 90]]
import numpy as np

A = np.array([[10, 20, 30],
              [40, 50, 60],
              [70, 80, 90]])

vector = A.flatten()

print("Flattened Vector:", vector)
print("Total Pixel Intensity:", np.sum(A))
